# NFC service scanner dictionary - an EXAMPLE (Galtzagorriak MINIX, #451)
#
# The scanner sends "SELECT <AID>" for every line below, one after the
# other, and lists the ones the card answers to.  Nothing else is sent:
# no READ, no PIN, no authentication.  The file is read a line at a time.
#
# Your own copy: /home/flipper/nfc/assets/aid_scan.nfc (used instead of
# this one when it is there).  Copy this file there and add your lines.
#
# Format:
#   # comment
#   [Group] one line telling what these services are (max 63 chars)
#   <AID in hex, 5 to 16 bytes> <name of the service>
#
# Only public application identifiers: no keys, no secrets (rule D.3).
# Sources: EMV and the card schemes' published AIDs, ICAO Doc 9303,
# ISO/IEC 18013-5, BSI TR-03110, NIST SP 800-73-4, FIDO U2F NFC, the
# OpenPGP card spec, gematik (eGK), NFC Forum Type 4 Tag, Calypso, and
# the AID lists of public reader tools (Proxmark3 aidlist.json).

